Kandor – patch 5: user-client selector redirects for OCLP's old AMDRadeonX5000.kext
Apply after patch 4. Author: JessiesFlying, with assistance from Claude (Anthropic)
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only

Tahoe's AMDRadeonX5000.kext dropped ForceLegacyMode (0x102), so the AMDAccelSharedUserClient selectors after it moved
down by one; OCLP's Vega userland on Tahoe calls getIOSurfaceInfo as 0x102 and RsrcAndXorByteFlag as 0x105 against the
old kext. Routes IOAccelSharedUserClient2::externalMethod (IOAcceleratorFamily2) and, only for that class and only when
the old kext is loaded (its ForceLegacyMode symbol exists), sends 0x102 with 1 scalar to 0x103 and 0x105 with a 12-byte
structure to 0x106. Kernel 22+, krygpu=AMD; disable with -krynoredirect. Replaces the IOConnect part of the shim wrapper.
Tested 21 Nov 2026 on Tahoe 26.7.2 (no failing 0x102/0x105 calls); no effect on Ventura to Sequoia, whose
userland calls 0x102 without scalars and 0x105 with 4 bytes (tested there too).

diff --git a/Kryptonite/Kryptonite/kern_hooks.cpp b/Kryptonite/Kryptonite/kern_hooks.cpp
index cbcdb83..cd2b487 100644
--- a/Kryptonite/Kryptonite/kern_hooks.cpp
+++ b/Kryptonite/Kryptonite/kern_hooks.cpp
@@ -12,3 +12,37 @@ int FunctionHooks::thunderboltShouldSkipEnumeration() {
     SYSLOG(moduleName, "Skipping thunderbolt enumeration...");
     return 0;
 }
+
+// Kandor (JessiesFlying, with assistance from Claude (Anthropic)), GPL-3.0-only:
+// Tahoe's AMDRadeonX5000.kext dropped ForceLegacyMode (selector 0x102) from AMDAccelSharedUserClient, so the
+// following selectors moved down by one. On Macs without AVX2, OCLP installs the old kext (0x102 = ForceLegacyMode,
+// 0x103 = getIOSurfaceInfo, 0x106 = RsrcAndXorByteFlag), but parts of its Tahoe userland (Metal, GL and video
+// drivers) call with Tahoe's numbers. Those calls fail with "count mismatch". Redirected here, only for that class
+// and only when the old kext is loaded (detected by its ForceLegacyMode symbol):
+//   0x102 with 1 scalar in             -> 0x103 getIOSurfaceInfo   (old 0x102 takes no scalars)
+//   0x105 with a 12-byte structure in  -> 0x106 RsrcAndXorByteFlag (old 0x105 AndXorByteFlag takes 4 bytes)
+// Calls in the old numbering are unaffected. Disable with -krynoredirect.
+mach_vm_address_t FunctionHooks::orgAccelSharedExternalMethod {0};
+bool FunctionHooks::oldX5000SharedUserClient {false};
+
+IOReturn FunctionHooks::accelSharedExternalMethod(IOUserClient *that, uint32_t selector, IOExternalMethodArguments *args,
+                                                  IOExternalMethodDispatch *dispatch, OSObject *target, void *reference) {
+    if (oldX5000SharedUserClient && that && args && (selector == 0x102 || selector == 0x105)) {
+        const OSMetaClass *meta = that->getMetaClass();
+        const char *name = meta ? meta->getClassName() : nullptr;
+        if (name && !strcmp(name, "AMDRadeonX5000_AMDAccelSharedUserClient")) {
+            uint32_t to = selector;
+            if (selector == 0x102 && args->scalarInputCount == 1) {
+                to = 0x103;
+            } else if (selector == 0x105 && args->scalarInputCount == 0 && args->structureInputSize == 12) {
+                to = 0x106;
+            }
+            if (to != selector) {
+                DBGLOG(moduleName, "redirect user-client selector 0x%x -> 0x%x", selector, to);
+                selector = to;
+                args->selector = to;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    return FunctionCast(accelSharedExternalMethod, orgAccelSharedExternalMethod)(that, selector, args, dispatch, target, reference);
+}
